CLAIM 4 VERIFICATION — `hideStepperAndActions` prop on `product-item/index.tsx`

## Check 1 — index.tsx (read in full, 233 lines) — CONFIRMED

- **Type/optionality**: `hideStepperAndActions?: boolean;` — `overrides/app/components/product-item/index.tsx:123`. Optional boolean, confirmed.
- **Default**: `hideStepperAndActions = false,` in the destructured props — `index.tsx:146`. Falsy by default, so omitting the prop cannot change existing behaviour.
- **Two `deliveryActions` render sites — BOTH gated** (this is the detail the task flagged as most likely to be broken; it is not):
  - Site 1, `index.tsx:174-176`:
    ```tsx
    {!hideStepperAndActions && deliveryActions && !product.bonusProductLineItem && (
      <HideOnMobile>{deliveryActions}</HideOnMobile>
    )}
    ```
  - Site 2, `index.tsx:179-181`:
    ```tsx
    {!hideStepperAndActions && deliveryActions && !product.bonusProductLineItem && (
      <HideOnDesktop>{deliveryActions}</HideOnDesktop>
    )}
    ```
  Both carry the identical `!hideStepperAndActions &&` guard. Confirmed by grep: `deliveryActions` appears exactly 4 times in the file — type decl (102), destructure (140), and these two render sites (174, 179) — no third, ungated site exists.
- **Stepper gated**, `index.tsx:185-197`: `{!hideStepperAndActions && !(isRemoving && product.bonusProductLineItem) && (product.bonusProductLineItem ? <BonusProductQuantity .../> : <ProductQuantityPicker .../>)}`.
- **`secondaryActions` gated** (single render site), `index.tsx:217`: `{!hideStepperAndActions && secondaryActions}`.
- **`primaryAction` gated** — bonus finding: like `deliveryActions`, `primaryAction` also has *two* render sites (desktop at `index.tsx:203`: `{!hideStepperAndActions && <HideOnMobile>{primaryAction}</HideOnMobile>}`; mobile at `index.tsx:221-225`: `{!hideStepperAndActions && (<HideOnDesktop><Box w={'full'}>{primaryAction}</Box></HideOnDesktop>)}`) — both gated too.

No incomplete gating found anywhere in the file. All 4 named slots, and specifically both `deliveryActions` sites, are suppressed together when the prop is true.

## Check 2 — index.test.tsx (read in full, 205 lines) — CONFIRMED

**(a) Suppression test**, `index.test.tsx:161-187` (`'hideStepperAndActions suppresses the stepper and every actions surface, and nothing throws'`):
```tsx
expect(() =>
  renderWithProviders(
    <ProductItem
      product={MOCK_LINE_ITEM}
      primaryAction={<button type="button">Remove</button>}
      secondaryActions={<button type="button">Edit</button>}
      deliveryActions={<span>Ship to store</span>}
      hideStepperAndActions
    />,
  ),
).not.toThrow();

expect(screen.queryByText('Quantity:')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' })).not.toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: 'Edit' })).not.toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.queryByText('Ship to store')).not.toBeInTheDocument();

expect(screen.getByAltText('Lilac Sand Silk Midi Dress')).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.getByText('Lilac Sand, One size')).toBeInTheDocument();
```
This goes well beyond "doesn't throw" — four real `queryBy*`/`.not.toBeInTheDocument()` DOM-absence assertions, plus two positive assertions proving the rest of the component still renders.

I independently verified this test is *structurally capable* of catching a one-of-two-sites bug, not just coincidentally passing: I read `overrides/app/components/responsive/index.tsx` and confirmed `HideOnMobile`/`HideOnDesktop` are pure Chakra `display` responsive-prop wrappers (`display={{base:'none', md:'block'}}` etc.) — both children **always mount in the DOM** regardless of viewport; jsdom doesn't remove either from the tree. Consequence: `screen.queryByText('Ship to store')` (singular) is a real trap for an incomplete fix — if only one of the two sites had been gated, the ungated site would still render exactly one "Ship to store" node, and `.not.toBeInTheDocument()` would fail (not silently pass); if *neither* site were gated, both would render, giving 2 matches, and `queryByText` (which throws on >1 match per Testing Library semantics) would throw, also failing the test. Same logic applies to `primaryAction`'s two sites via `queryByRole(...'Remove')`. So this single test is sufficient to catch both a fully-missed fix and a half-fixed (one-site-only) fix for `deliveryActions`/`primaryAction`.

**(b) Existing-caller-unaffected test**, `index.test.tsx:189-203` (`'every existing caller (hideStepperAndActions omitted) is unaffected — the stepper and actions still render'`):
```tsx
renderWithProviders(
  <ProductItem
    product={MOCK_LINE_ITEM}
    primaryAction={<button type="button">Remove</button>}
    secondaryActions={<button type="button">Edit</button>}
    deliveryActions={<span>Ship to store</span>}
  />,
);

expect(screen.getByText('Quantity:')).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.getAllByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' }).length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Edit' })).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.getAllByText('Ship to store').length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```
Real positive-presence assertions, prop omitted entirely (relying on the `= false` default). Correctly uses plural `getAllBy*`/`.length > 0` for the two dual-render-site slots (`primaryAction`, `deliveryActions`) and singular `getBy*` for the single-render-site slots (stepper text, `secondaryActions`) — internally consistent with the component's actual structure found in Check 1.

## Check 3 — index.stories.tsx — CONFIRMED (with one minor gap noted)

`GiftCard` story exists, `index.stories.tsx:173-180`:
```tsx
export const GiftCard: Story = {
  args: {
    product: MOCK_LINE_ITEM,
    primaryAction: <button type="button">Remove</button>,
    secondaryActions: <button type="button">Edit</button>,
    hideStepperAndActions: true,
  },
};
```
Minor observation (not disqualifying): the story does not pass `deliveryActions`, so it doesn't visually demonstrate that slot being suppressed — only `primaryAction`/`secondaryActions` are shown being hidden. The `deliveryActions` half of the behaviour is proven only by the Vitest test in Check 2, not by this story. Since the task's ask was just to confirm the story exists and passes the prop, this is satisfied, but flagging it since deliveryActions was the specifically-suspected weak point.

Bonus (not required, found while in the folder): `overrides/app/components/product-item/index.stories.test.tsx:194-208` has its own `'GiftCard-equivalent'` test running the same scenario through the real (unmocked) provider chain, asserting `queryByRole('button',{name:'Remove'/'Edit'}).not.toBeInTheDocument()` — same caveat, doesn't touch `deliveryActions` either.

## Check 4 — real test run — PASS

```
$ npx vitest run overrides/app/components/product-item/index.test.tsx

